Description: Fix SyntaxError on Python < 3.12 caused by a backslash inside
 an f-string expression part
 The expression part of the outer f-string contains a nested f-string
 with escaped double quotes (\"...\"), i.e. a backslash inside the {...}
 expression. This is only valid starting with Python 3.12 (PEP 701:
 f-strings without the previous backslash restriction). On Python 3.11
 and earlier this raises "SyntaxError: f-string expression part cannot
 include a backslash" in _location_paragraphs, which prevents the
 Django app from starting at all (import of collection_pdf.py fails
 immediately).
Upstream-bug: https://github.com/seanmorley15/AdventureLog/issues
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-08-12
